k partitioning with LVM, user setup, and OpenSSH installation. As a bonus, the guide also covers installing Apache2, editing the default index.html with nano, and verifying the web server is accessible via the server's local IP address.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vjiR7iUMzZg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T12:33:22.000Z"},{"id":"XCvwxil6k","title":"Ubuntu\u2019s AI Push, AMD Fixes HDMI 2.1, Valve Keeps Winning & VPN Laws Get Wild","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u4ADY0Sgzuc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ubuntu-s-ai-push-amd-fixes-hdmi-2-1-valve-keeps-winning-vpn-laws-get-wild-xcvwxil6k","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u4ADY0Sgzuc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-03T16:46:45.000Z"},{"id":"pFUuRxKbP","title":"Let's Sneak Some VPN Bans into Age Verification Laws","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wK8erYSp354","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/let-s-sneak-some-vpn-bans-into-age-verification-laws-pfuurxkbp","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wK8erYSp354/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-02T21:04:44.000Z"},{"id":"g9YnLi4zO","title":"Copy Fail: This Exploit Gives Root Access on Linux","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_bckyC6w9f4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/copy-fail-this-exploit-gives-root-access-on-linux-g9ynli4zo","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_bckyC6w9f4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T02:27:52.000Z"},{"id":"hsk9f5mcH","title":"GitHub: MASSIVE CVE, Bugs Delete Code & AI Controversy","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q1I5m6cQNlY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/github-massive-cve-bugs-delete-code-ai-controversy-hsk9f5mch","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/q1I5m6cQNlY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"aOtlrbCpK","title":"Proton Fights for Privacy as Linux Age Verification Expands","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RE51m6JnYMo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/proton-fights-for-privacy-as-linux-age-verification-expands-aotlrbcpk","summary":"Proton CEO Andy Yen has published a blog post arguing that current age verification proposals worldwide threaten online anonymity and privacy. He acknowledges that protecting children online is a real concern, but warns that broad age verification mandates would effectively end anonymous internet use. Key arguments include: collected identity data inevitably gets leaked (citing Discord's 70,000-user breach and the EU/UK age verification app being bypassed within hours), third-party age verification companies face incentives to monetize user data, and big tech companies like Apple and Google cannot be trusted as gatekeepers given their history of data exploitation. Yen also calls out Meta for lobbying in favor of age verification not to protect children, but to offload responsibility. If age verification must exist, Proton argues it should be client-side only, use no facial scans or uploaded IDs, be fully anonymized, end-to-end encrypted, and built on open source code. The post also touches on how these laws could extend beyond age to nationality-based internet blocking.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RE51m6JnYMo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"rEZpflIfE","title":"How to Dual Boot Windows 11 and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GnXPJkH55Vg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-dual-boot-windows-11-and-ubuntu-26-04-lts-rezpflife","summary":"Step-by-step guide to dual booting Ubuntu 26.04 LTS alongside Windows 10/11. Covers downloading the Ubuntu ISO, flashing it to a USB drive with Balena Etcher, shrinking the Windows C partition using Disk Management to free up space, configuring BIOS boot order and disabling Secure Boot, running the Ubuntu installer with manual partitioning (ext4, root mount point), setting up the GRUB bootloader, and verifying both OSes boot correctly. Also includes post-install tips like installing VLC, GIMP, LibreOffice, and Steam.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GnXPJkH55Vg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Ti2ziqbUn","title":"Are You Ready for Linux? (Check Before You Switch)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3K8ktHEH96o","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/are-you-ready-for-linux-check-before-you-switch--ti2ziqbun","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/3K8ktHEH96o/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-22T22:59:40.000Z"},{"id":"gjDppN7j1","title":"Linux and open source weekly news roundup covering kernel changes, security, and age verification laws","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RdCdVntdAew","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/us-linux-age-laws-explode-fedora-trouble-xorg-bugs-eu-privacy-mess-more-gjdppn7j1","summary":"A weekly Linux and open source news roundup covering: Linux 7.1 dropping i486 and Russian Baikal CPU support; a new fault-tolerant FTRFS filesystem proposal for radiation environments; Btrfs performance and reliability improvements in Linux 7.1; five new Xorg/Xwayland CVEs patched in Xserver 21.1.22; SDL banning AI-generated code contributions; GhostBSD moving to FreeBSD 15 and XLibre as default display server; Mozilla announcing open-source AI client Thunderbolt; Linux Mint 23 plans based on Ubuntu 26.04; an improved NTFS driver merged into Linux 7.1; Fedora 44 delayed to April 28 due to blocker bugs; KDE Plasma 6.7 adding per-screen virtual desktops and Wayland session restore; US bill HR8250 (Parents Decide Act) proposing OS-level age verification with major privacy implications; the EU's age verification app being hacked in under two minutes; and France planning to migrate government systems from Windows to Linux.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RdCdVntdAew/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-19T20:30:39.000Z"},{"id":"WqxaOEZUN","title":"Disable YouTube Shorts in YOUR Feed","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l8DgffGapKs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/disable-youtube-shorts-in-your-feed-wqxaoezun","summary":"YouTube has added a new method to disable Shorts from your feed on mobile. By navigating to Settings > Time Management and setting the daily limit to 0 minutes, you can prevent Shorts from appearing in your feed. You may need to refresh or tap a Short once before the change takes effect.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/l8DgffGapKs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-18T15:58:52.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["sebastianlague","windowsdevelopers","csdojo","noboilerplate","entreprenueropp"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","devtools"],"similar":[{"id":"sebastianlague","handle":"sebastianlague","name":"Sebastian Lague","is_squad":false,"x":-5.4082,"y":-8.4359,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":61,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--rxa5CpKA--/f_auto/v1727446540/logos/sebastianlague","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.727646,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.016393,"avg_read_time":23.229508,"tag_diversity":0.52459},"top_tags_preview":[["game-development",34],["unity",23],["graphics-programming",11]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-4.4265,0.8235],"cadence_depth":[-3.1324,8.9853],"hype_variety":[3.8676,-4.1618],"title_style":[-0.1029,-2.3824]}},{"id":"windowsdevelopers","handle":"windowsdevelopers","name":"Windows Developer","is_squad":false,"x":-6.1148,"y":-8.3005,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":111,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--lAMBCxTU--/f_auto/v1725035411/logos/windowsdevelopers","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.282233,"median_upvotes